# Skytraine Opportunity Network — Environment Variables

# --- Database (required) ---
# PostgreSQL connection string. For V1 use a managed Postgres (Vercel Postgres, Neon, or Supabase).
#
# Supabase note: use the TRANSACTION-MODE pooler (port 6543) with pgbouncer=true and
# connection_limit=1. The session-mode pooler (port 5432) caps at 15 concurrent
# connections and is exhausted by serverless (Vercel) instances -> causes "(EMAXCONNSESSION)
# max clients reached" and login failures. The app (src/lib/prisma.ts and prisma/seed.ts)
# passes ssl:{ rejectUnauthorized:false } to the PrismaPg adapter so pg uses plain "require"
# TLS instead of escalating to verify-full (which fails against Supabase's cert chain).
# Percent-encode special characters in the password (e.g. ? -> %3F, # -> %23, $ -> %24).
#
# format: postgresql://<user>:<encoded-password>@<host>:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:6543/database?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1"

# --- NextAuth (required) ---
# A long, random secret used to sign auth session tokens. Never expose publicly.
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="generate-a-long-random-string"
# The canonical public URL of the app. Set to your Vercel domain in production.
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# --- Admin seed account (used by `npm run db:seed`) ---
ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL="admin@skytraine.com"
ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD="change-this-to-a-strong-password"
ADMIN_SEED_NAME="Skytraine Admin"
